<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zawaya</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Zawaya are the scholarly and religious tribes of Moorish society in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mauritania">Mauritania</a> and the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a>, mostly of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanhaja">Sanhaja</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> origin. Unlike the Hassani warrior tribes, they devoted themselves to Islamic learning, teaching, trade and herding. Their defeat by the Hassani in the Char Bouba war of the 1670s fixed a social order in which they paid tribute to warrior <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a> while keeping great religious prestige.</p></div>
